    // waste-floor pressure with a full-stream coupling between remaining
    // item demand and the fresh bin's post residual. Early in the stream
    // there is enough future demand to fill any residual, so new bins are
    // cheap; as remaining demand shrinks below the residual, the cost of
    // stranding that space rises super-linearly. This sharpens bin-count
    // compaction by refusing to strand space the stream can no longer fill.
    if bin_residual == bin_capacity {
